\description{
A drop-in replacement for \code{\link[ggplot2:geom_histogram]{ggplot2::geom_histogram()}} (and by extension
\code{\link[ggplot2:geom_bar]{ggplot2::geom_bar()}}) that renders each bar as a rounded rectangle
("chicklet") instead of a sharp rectangle. Implemented as a real
\code{ggproto} (\code{GeomChickletHistogram}) inheriting from \link[ggplot2:Geom]{ggplot2::GeomBar}
and using \link[ggplot2:Stat]{ggplot2::StatBin} for stat computation, so it supports the
full bar/histogram aesthetic set (\code{x}/\code{y}, \code{weight}, \code{fill}, \code{colour},
\code{linewidth}, \code{linetype}, \code{alpha}), horizontal orientation
(\code{orientation = "y"} / \code{\link[ggplot2:coord_flip]{ggplot2::coord_flip()}}), faceting, and
position adjustments (\code{"stack"}, \code{"identity"}, \code{\link[ggplot2:position_dodge]{ggplot2::position_dodge()}}).
}
\details{
All four corners of every bar are rounded — this matches the behaviour
of the other chicklet geoms (\code{\link[=geom_chicklet]{geom_chicklet()}}, \code{\link[=geom_rrect]{geom_rrect()}}). For
typical baseline-aligned histograms this means the bottom edges sit
slightly off the x-axis baseline (by \code{radius}); reduce \code{radius} if
that gap is visually distracting.

Polar / non-linear coordinate systems are not supported; in those
cases the bars fall back to ordinary (sharp-cornered) rendering
inherited from \link[ggplot2:Geom]{ggplot2::GeomBar}.
}
